      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلْبِيبٌ</span></b>  The <i>portion of the clothes that is at the
part called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَب</span>: a subst., like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمْتِينٌ</span>: (K:) pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلَابِيبُ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخَذَ بِتَلْبِيبِهِ</span> <i>He drew together
his clothes at the bosom, and seized him, dragging
him along:</i> (T:) <i>he took him by the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَّة</span>: you
also say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اخذ بِتَلَابِيبِهِ</span>. (TA.) See also 2 and 5.

